; MidiRealJumps -- the danger levels' jumps with the user's own songs (the
; user on Hamiller, 21.11.: the General MIDI music "ran haywire shortly
; after the fort fell"). Like MidiCamd, but with the songs of the user's
; install, copied into dist/Test/real-songs for the run (never into the
; repo) and deleted again afterwards. orig01 is a desert map (AD1); 8 s
; into it a jump as ZMusicEngine makes them (ZOD_MIDI_TESTJUMP):
; (1) to the desert's FORT place 335.77 s (step 40292): 35 s before the
;     song's end, so the loop back to its start follows in the same run;
; (2) to the desert's CALM place 60 s (step 7200) -- where the music goes
;     15 s after one's own fort fell.
; Then on the Mac: tools/zmu_midi_check.py build/autotest/MidiRealJumps.serial
;      dist/Test/real-songs --real --log build/autotest/MidiRealJumps.run
; LIMIT 600
; SERIAL_RAW
FailAt 1000
Wait 5
Echo "=== machine ===" >DEV:Test/auto.log
CPU >>DEV:Test/auto.log
Delete >NIL: DEV:Test/zod-#?
MakeDir >NIL: DEV:Zod/music
Copy DEV:Test/real-songs/#?.zmu DEV:Zod/music/ QUIET
Echo "=== (1) software, orig01, a jump to the FORT place 335.77 s ===" >>DEV:Test/auto.log
SetEnv ZOD_MIDI_TESTJUMP 40292@8
Run >NIL: Execute DEV:Test/RunZodMidi rj1 60 -o -m Data/Campaing/Z_original/p02_bb_orig01.map
Execute DEV:Test/WaitDone DEV:Test/zod-rj1.done
Type DEV:Test/zod-rj1.log >>DEV:Test/auto.log
Echo "=== (2) software, orig01, a jump to the CALM place 60 s ===" >>DEV:Test/auto.log
SetEnv ZOD_MIDI_TESTJUMP 7200@8
Run >NIL: Execute DEV:Test/RunZodMidi rj2 40 -o -m Data/Campaing/Z_original/p02_bb_orig01.map
Execute DEV:Test/WaitDone DEV:Test/zod-rj2.done
Type DEV:Test/zod-rj2.log >>DEV:Test/auto.log
UnSetEnv ZOD_MIDI_TESTJUMP
Delete >NIL: DEV:Zod/music/#?.zmu
Delete >NIL: DEV:Zod/music
Echo "=== done ===" >>DEV:Test/auto.log
Echo >DEV:Test/AutoDone done
